ELECTRON IMPACT IONIZATION OF HYDROGEN 
hionize4.nc

ELECTRON RECOMBINATION OF HYDROGEN
hrecombine4.nc

Generated these from ehr4.dat which is a trivially modified version
of the ADAS based data file obtained from Stuart Loch in connection
with the calculations described in S. D. Loch et al., Plasma Phys.
Control. Fusion 51, 105006 (2009).  The fundamental data underlying
these calculations are much more accurate than those of the old
model (ehr3.dat).  However, the collisional radiative coefficients, 
particularly the ionization and recombination rates, are not
dramatically different for typical tokamak parameters.  There are
known problems with this file, particularly the "continuum electron loss"
behavior at low electron temperature, that require the user to exercise
caution before incorporating them into a particular calculation.  The
population coefficients for n >= 6 are the same as those in ehr3.dat.

