DEUTERIUM DEUTERIUM ELASTIC SCATTERING
dd_neut.nc

  --Version 3.0--
These data are for use with the BGK method and have the T**0.25 scaling
for the reaction rate originally proposed by May (see the Neutral-
Neutral Elastic Scattering section of the User's Manual) and implemented
in EIRENE.  The numerical value of the rate corresponds to
5.4241e-10*T**0.25, where T is the deuterium temperature in eV.
Note that the data in the files is for the specific energy; the 
corresponding absolute temperature range is 1.e-3 to 100 eV.
The origin of the files themselves is not documented.  However,
an equivalent file can be easily constructed by hand since only
two data values are needed to reproduce this scaling, given the
use of log interpolation (and that the sigv_max is not needed for
this reaction type).  Note also that these rates should be
replaced by constant values.  In fact, the User's Manual has already
been revised to reflect this change.

